  comment-2578074o = {WHO has conducted a study on the SLRs of published evidence regarding the potential effects of exposure RF-EMF on humans
Deficit model theory - experts assume that non-experts will accept science once they are properly informed, the ideas has been challenged in the science communication literature
Factors such as social norms and trust in institutions contribute more to acceptance of science than objective knoledge
Perceptions of lack of agency that experts did not anticipate (providers switched to 5G without asking the customers)
And exposure to 5G happens no matter what.

non-experts cannot be characterised solely by their lack of knowledge about technical aspects or even their enjoyment of technology, instead their perceptions are changed by beliefs about regulation, trust attitudes towards technology and perceived agency
